{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unpleasing-starchy-teal","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Purpose\nThis ticket is the mechanism-ratchet admission for the test helper `tests/_python_child.py` (kind `test_helper`). The helper is permanent test infrastructure, delivered by smoking-bereft-boar (c7b2-e4ed-37fd-4f60):\n- `dead_pid()` replaces 4 duplicated dead-pid helpers.\n- `spawn_python()`/`stop()` give lock-holder tests the interpreter's own pid behind a Windows venv launcher.\n\nThe repo has one convention for admitting a mechanism added after the baseline froze (`docs/architecture.md` §\"Mechanism-delta ratchet\"; `src/rebar/_commands/sunset_markers.py`). A `# mechanism-ok:` marker at the definition site names a ticket, and rebar refuses to close that ticket while the marker remains. The marker on line 1 of `tests/_python_child.py` names this ticket. Precedent: added-ephemeral-seaslug.\n\n## Lifecycle\n- This ticket stays `open` and unclaimed as long as `tests/_python_child.py` exists. Do not work it and do not close it.\n- It closes only when a future change removes the helper. That change deletes the marker in the same commit and runs `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale`.","id":"1503-b191-89ec-4e13","parent_id":"","priority":4,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Keep tests/_python_child.py test helper admitted (permanent; stays open while helper exists)"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795326340507953001,"uuid":"254c89cd-3104-47da-a649-c0cfdef08463"}